  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "This paper proposes a gate-based quantum circuit equivalence-checking flow that first performs up to r = 16 random simulation runs and then applies a decision-diagram-based G◦I◦G' routine. On the benchmark suite from RevLib/Qiskit, the proposed method often reduces runtime from >3600 s for the state-of-the-art checker to seconds or less on non-equivalent cases, with simulation success probabilities around 0.80–1.00 for the perturbed benchmarks in Table III.",
